// expect: refuse E_TypeMismatch
// A record REST binds a residual its writer PROVED whole — the closed
// partner's fields are the entire set — so a field name outside it is
// provably absent, exactly as it is on the record itself. Demanding one
// must refuse, not widen.
//
// SEEN RED at pin bc516cf945bb, twice and in the worst way: `rest.nosuch`
// checked clean and ran to exit 0, and the name below — chosen to sort
// BEFORE the real field — ran to exit 2, which is `b`'s value. A field
// that does not exist returned a field that does.
//
// The control was already correct: the same unknown name on a plain
// closed record is E_TypeMismatch at the access. This fixture holds the
// residual path to the verdict the record path always gave.
fn make() = ({a: 1, b: 2})
fn main(q) = {
  let {a, ...rest} = make()
  rest.aa
}
